 "findings": [
  "Daily AI hours explain most of the variation in weekly time saved (R\u00b2 about 0.76) and productivity (about 0.56). Tool, country, field, income and cost add almost nothing.",
  "Each extra AI hour a day goes with about 1.7 more hours saved per week.",
  "Returns diminish: median time saved per AI hour falls from 0.38 h at <=1h to 0.26 h at >6h.",
  "Accuracy ratings do not rise with usage (rank correlation +0.05).",
  "Paid and free users report similar results, and students and professionals look alike."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "The data is self-reported and observational, so these are associations, not causal effects.",
  "The patterns are unusually clean for survey data, which suggests the dataset is partly synthetic.",
  "Individuals vary by about 2 hours a week around the expected value; use the tool for rough planning."
 ]
